<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Troglita</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 530s–550s</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Iohannes Troglita</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Troglita was a Byzantine general sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> in 546, after Berber revolts and army mutinies had shaken the new Praetorian Prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. In campaigns from 546 to 548 he defeated the Laguatan and the Moorish leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antalas">Antalas</a>, restoring Byzantine control. His wars are celebrated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> epic Iohannis by the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corippus">Corippus</a>, a main source for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> peoples of the time.</p></div>
